A||||10||maryjane||U.S. Flags confiscated||||9||
Z||000000||maryjane||09-17-2001||10:47 PM||||Anybody see this? Seems a company in Boca Raton, Fla decided that people couldn't display American flags or other symbols of Nationalism at their desks last week. Reason given- might offend persons of other ethnic backgrounds. The media got hold of it & they did an about face later, but not before at least one person quit, when a supervisor was sent to confiscate the flags. EXTRA, EXTRA,<BR>Read all about it. <A HREF="http://www.gopbi.com/partners/pbpost/epaper/editions/saturday/business_3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gopbi.com/partners/pbpost/epaper/editions/saturday/business_3.html</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Taijiguy||09-17-2001||10:51 PM||||I saw this in a hackers newsgroup. The poster was soliciting people ("no-balls-ing" people actually) to hack their web page. Apparently the company actually started handing out flags to people who wanted them. In my opinion, this is the United States, and if someone else don't like me sporting a flag on my desk, they not only can kiss my ass, they can find someplace else to live.||||reg||8
